  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be a point on the hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, in the first quadrant such that the area of triangle formed by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and the two foci of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></math>. Then, the square of the distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> from the origin is",
    "image": null
  },
